Subject: [PATCH] GS GPU renderer: a load into a buffer kept as field pictures keeps the pictures (TODO 205)

After a state load in Antarctica the GPU renderer showed, now and then for a frame, the whole picture under red and
green bands (the depth buffer's bytes as colours). With both fields as moments the display buffers are kept as their
field pictures alone; their own textures are not drawn. The game's trail reads the previous display buffer at 1024
rows, so that buffer's rows past 448 share pages with the other display buffer - the scene's depth buffer every
second frame - and those depth draws made it stale. Reading it then loaded the stale cells (rows the pictures never
show) and made every field picture invalid, so the trail sampled the buffer's own texture: local memory as it was at
the last load (after a state load, an old depth buffer), blended over the frame.

The cells a load brings in now go into the buffer's valid field pictures too, which stay its pictures. A load of the
whole buffer (one not at a page boundary) still makes them invalid, as before.

Checked on the user's state user_199 (Antarctica), GPU alone, 7 shots in the window where it showed (+90 to +210
VBlanks after the load), 10 runs each way on this PC: scrambled frames 0 of 70 with the fix, 4 of 70 (plus several
milder ones) with PS2X_GPU_KEEP_PICTURES=0; every shot with the fix within 2 of the median picture.
PS2X_GPU_KEEP_PICTURES=0: all made invalid, as before.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp
index f21cb80..e1661f6 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp
@@ -1610,6 +1610,8 @@ struct GSGpuRenderer::Impl
     bool stats = false;
     uint64_t statBatches = 0u, statDraws = 0u, statPrims = 0u, statVertices = 0u, statSkipped = 0u, statCulled = 0u, statUploads = 0u,
              statLoadRows = 0u, statWriteRows = 0u, statFeedback = 0u, statSyncs = 0u, statDownloads = 0u, statReadbacks = 0u, statReadbackPages = 0u;
+    uint64_t statPicturesKept = 0u;                // (TODO 205) loads whose cells went into the field pictures too
+    std::vector<std::array<int, 4>> loadedRects; // (ensureLoaded: the GL rectangles it loaded)
     std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point statStart = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
     // GPU time of the passes (elapsed-time queries, read when they are done): draws, field
     // pictures, loads from local memory, write-backs, presentation.
@@ -2939,6 +2941,7 @@ void GSGpuRenderer::Impl::ensureLoaded(Target &t)
             const int x1 = std::min(static_cast<int>(end) * pw, t.width);
             glScissor(x0 * t.sx, static_cast<int>(cy) * ph * t.sy, (x1 - x0) * t.sx, ph * t.sy);
             glDrawArrays(GL_TRIANGLES, 0, 3);
+            loadedRects.push_back({x0 * t.sx, static_cast<int>(cy) * ph * t.sy, (x1 - x0) * t.sx, ph * t.sy});
             rowsLoaded += static_cast<uint64_t>(ph) * static_cast<uint64_t>(x1 - x0) / static_cast<uint64_t>(t.width);
             cx = end;
         }
@@ -2946,7 +2949,29 @@ void GSGpuRenderer::Impl::ensureLoaded(Target &t)
     timeEnd();
     std::fill(t.staleCells.begin(), t.staleCells.end(), uint8_t{0u});
     t.anyStale = false;
-    std::fill(std::begin(t.shadowValid), std::end(t.shadowValid), false); // (the buffer changed under its field pictures)
+    // The buffer changed under its field pictures: (TODO 205) the cells loaded go into the pictures that hold it as well,
+    // which stay its pictures. Before, any load made them all invalid, and what read the buffer then had its own texture -
+    // with both fields as moments never drawn (local memory's content at the last load: after a state load, the depth
+    // buffer of the scene before). Transformers' display buffer is read by its trail at 1024 rows: its rows past 448 share
+    // pages with the other display buffer, the scene's depth buffer every second frame, and those draws made it stale -
+    // the trail then blended in that old memory, a frame of red and green bands now and then after a state load.
+    // PS2X_GPU_KEEP_PICTURES=0: all made invalid, as before.
+    static const bool keepPictures = envFlag("PS2X_GPU_KEEP_PICTURES", true);
+    bool anyPicture = false;
+    for (int k = 0; k < kShadows; ++k)
+        anyPicture = anyPicture || (t.shadowValid[k] && t.shadow[k]);
+    if (keepPictures && anyPicture && !whole)
+    {
+        glMemoryBarrier(GL_ALL_BARRIER_BITS); // (the load's image stores finished before the copies)
+        for (int k = 0; k < kShadows; ++k)
+            if (t.shadowValid[k] && t.shadow[k])
+                for (const auto &r : loadedRects)
+                    glCopyImageSubData(t.tex, GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, r[0], r[1], 0, t.shadow[k], GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, r[0], r[1], 0, r[2], r[3], 1);
+        ++statPicturesKept;
+    }
+    else
+        std::fill(std::begin(t.shadowValid), std::end(t.shadowValid), false);
+    loadedRects.clear();
     for (uint32_t cy = 0; cy < t.cellsY && cy < t.depthRows.size(); ++cy)
         if (cellRowLoaded[cy])
             t.depthRows[cy] = kDepthTexture; // (and under its native depth)
@@ -6665,6 +6690,8 @@ void GSGpuRenderer::Impl::printStats()
                  static_cast<unsigned long long>(statLoadRows), static_cast<unsigned long long>(statWriteRows),
                  static_cast<unsigned long long>(statFeedback), static_cast<unsigned long long>(statSyncs),
                  static_cast<unsigned long long>(statDownloads), targets.size());
+    std::fprintf(stderr, "[gpu]   field pictures kept through a load: %llu\n", static_cast<unsigned long long>(statPicturesKept));
+    statPicturesKept = 0u;
     std::fprintf(stderr, "[gpu]   read-backs and local copies: %llu, %llu of their pages drawn by the GPU\n",
                  static_cast<unsigned long long>(statReadbacks), static_cast<unsigned long long>(statReadbackPages));
     statReadbacks = statReadbackPages = 0u;
